```java
@Service
class PricingService { // shared logic, depends on neither side
    BigDecimal total(Order order) {
        return order.getItems().stream()
            .map(Item::getPrice)
            .reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add);
    }
}

@Service
class OrderService {
    private final PricingService pricing;
    OrderService(PricingService pricing) { this.pricing = pricing; }
}

@Service
class PaymentService {
    private final PricingService pricing; // both depend on the shared bean
    PaymentService(PricingService pricing) { this.pricing = pricing; }
}
```
With the shared logic pulled out, neither service depends on the other and the cycle is gone.

```java
@Service
class OrderService {
    private final PaymentService paymentService;

    // @Lazy injects a proxy and defers real creation, breaking the cycle
    OrderService(@Lazy PaymentService paymentService) {
        this.paymentService = paymentService;
    }
}
```
This compiles and runs, but the tight coupling remains — prefer refactoring when you can.

```java
@Service
class OrderService {
    // Depends on a concrete class -> violates Dependency Inversion
    private final StripePaymentService payment = new StripePaymentService();

    void checkout(Order o) { payment.charge(o); }
}
```

```java
interface PaymentService { void charge(Order o); }

@Service
class StripePaymentService implements PaymentService {
    public void charge(Order o) { /* call Stripe */ }
}

@Service
class OrderService {
    private final PaymentService payment; // depends on the interface
    OrderService(PaymentService payment) { this.payment = payment; }

    void checkout(Order o) { payment.charge(o); }
}
```
Now swapping Stripe for PayPal means adding one bean, with no change to OrderService.

```java
interface OrderRepository {
    Optional<Order> findById(Long id);
    void save(Order order);
}

@Repository
class JpaOrderRepository implements OrderRepository {
    private final EntityManager em;
    JpaOrderRepository(EntityManager em) { this.em = em; }
    public Optional<Order> findById(Long id) { return Optional.ofNullable(em.find(Order.class, id)); }
    public void save(Order order) { em.persist(order); }
}

@Repository
@Profile("test")
class InMemoryOrderRepository implements OrderRepository {
    private final Map<Long, Order> store = new HashMap<>();
    public Optional<Order> findById(Long id) { return Optional.ofNullable(store.get(id)); }
    public void save(Order order) { store.put(order.id(), order); }
}

@Service
class OrderService {
    private final OrderRepository repository; // interface, not a concrete class
    OrderService(OrderRepository repository) { this.repository = repository; }
}
```
